<title>UK: Kenwood shares fall after bid talk dampened.</title>
<headline>Kenwood shares fall after bid talk dampened.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Kenwood Appliances Plc fell on Tuesday after the company dampened bid speculation and announced first-half pre-tax profits more than halved to 3.3 million stg from 7.4 million. At 0918 GMT, Kenwood shares were down 8p at 225-1/2p.</p>
<p>The company, which faces moves by rebel shareholders aimed at soliciting a buyer, noted the interest expressed by Pifco Holdings Plc as reported in the Financial Times but said no formal offer had been received.</p>
<p>Pifco shares were unchanged at 283p.</p>
<p>-- Brian Killen, London newsroom 44 171 542 7972</p>
